From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 14:02:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] subprocess: Initializes the outputs in test_hang.

bs_subprocess_terminated() sets them only when the subprocess terminated;
the first call (still running) left them uninitialized, which GCC flags
with -O2 (-Wmaybe-uninitialized).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/subprocess.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/subprocess.c b/src/subprocess.c
index cab45aa..7979412 100644
--- a/src/subprocess.c
+++ b/src/subprocess.c
@@ -940,7 +940,7 @@ void test_hang(bs_test_t *test_ptr)
     BS_TEST_VERIFY_NEQ(test_ptr, NULL, sp_ptr);
     BS_TEST_VERIFY_TRUE(test_ptr, bs_subprocess_start(sp_ptr));
 
-    int exit_status, signal_number;
+    int exit_status = 0, signal_number = 0;
     BS_TEST_VERIFY_FALSE(
         test_ptr,
         bs_subprocess_terminated(sp_ptr, &exit_status, &signal_number));
-- 
2.56.0

